# Block30 mutation plan

The runner must reject altered models at their load-bearing predicates.  It
must not count stored expected booleans.

1. replace an orbit relation with a coordinate-named test;
2. use an immediate reverse direction in one word;
3. delete one of the four route steps;
4. change one step so the endpoint is not a facing PairFrame;
5. revisit a Record center within one arm;
6. collide the two arms;
7. target one of `0,f,2f,3f,A,B`;
8. overwrite rather than QND-preserve the current Locked word;
9. replace one required Blank input by a Locked block;
10. corrupt a literal straight append factor;
11. corrupt a literal perpendicular turn factor;
12. alias two decoded pair controls;
13. drop the STOP complement;
14. choose the route as a function of `lambda`;
15. claim the two valid chiralities are one path;
16. claim the pair-level controller is already a nearest-neighbor law;
17. promote the bounded result to reuse, renewal, cadence, gravity, axiom
    need, audit retention, obligation retirement, or TOE movement.

Both signs of `f cross g` are valid models.  Flipping chirality is therefore a
positive multiplicity control, not a mutation that should fail.
